WHAT FIRES A PIN. tools/twatch.py, pin_shadow() -> pin_now(). All of:
  - tier is `full` (the broadest nested tier; nothing narrower may qualify one)
  - no red the current pin does not already carry, and the allowlist is EMPTY
    so nothing at all is waived today
  - a LIVE self-host fixedpoint job in THIS run, passing. Never waivable: a
    compiler that cannot reproduce itself must not become anyone's ground
  - two consecutive qualifying shas (PIN_STREAK_K = 2)
  - the checkout is still DETACHED at the sha the tier ran on
  - the tree is clean, and compiler/pascal26 still hashes to the binary the run
    recorded in compiler_sha256
  - the run did not straddle a compiler change, and produced a real measurement

Every one of those fails CLOSED. The failure mode is "did not pin", which is
what the last month did anyway.

